<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dukla Pass</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dukla Pass is a low pass in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-mountains">Carpathian Mountains</a> on the border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a>. In September to November 1944 Soviet and Czechoslovak forces fought a costly battle there in an attempt to reach the Slovak National Uprising. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/1st-czechoslovak-army-corps">1st Czechoslovak Army Corps</a> lost thousands of men, and the battle is commemorated by a memorial on the pass.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dukla-pass.jpg" alt="Dukla Pass" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This file was created and uploaded by User:Szater Ten plik został stworzony i dodany przez Wikipedystę:Szater Szater ... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dukla_Pass_battle_monument_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
